1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,420
We are the Roseguard Imperial Knights.

2
00:00:04,840 --> 00:00:07,860
We heard a hero was headed into this cave and hurried here.

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:09,200
Oh, that's so.

4
00:00:09,420 --> 00:00:14,580
The knights under the command of Captain Rosalie are engaging the Demon Lord's forces at Olga Fortress.

5
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:16,460
We ask that you come with us.

6
00:00:18,280 --> 00:00:18,760
Okay.

7
00:00:19,540 --> 00:00:21,640
We did come here to save the world after all.

8
00:00:22,160 --> 00:00:23,160
So let's get going.

9
00:00:24,420 --> 00:00:25,660
The rumors are true.

10
00:00:25,720 --> 00:00:27,480
It's like having a hundred more men.

11
00:00:27,480 --> 00:00:30,040
Is there anybody in this world who doesn't need my help?

12
00:00:30,480 --> 00:00:32,580
I was hoping for like five seconds of downtime.

13
00:00:33,660 --> 00:00:36,560
We will gladly lead you all the way to Olga Fortress.

14
00:00:36,600 --> 00:00:37,820
I'd rather you didn't.

15
00:00:37,980 --> 00:00:39,520
Just tell me what direction it's in.

16
00:00:40,080 --> 00:00:41,140
North by Northwest.

17
00:00:42,260 --> 00:00:44,220
Oh, he really can fly.

18
00:00:44,480 --> 00:00:46,680
No ordinary mortal can do that.

19
00:00:46,760 --> 00:00:48,460
That's why heroes are better than us.

20
00:00:48,600 --> 00:00:50,600
I believe he can bring down Beelbub.

21
00:00:50,960 --> 00:00:52,840
Who's this Beelbub you're talking about?

22
00:00:52,840 --> 00:00:55,140
A demon that looks like a giant fly.

23
00:00:55,140 --> 00:01:01,080
A swarm of those disgusting creatures led by Beelbub is causing massive casualties at Olga Fortress.

24
00:01:01,320 --> 00:01:02,920
So we're in for midair combat.

25
00:01:03,440 --> 00:01:04,940
We'll do a little recon first.

26
00:01:05,440 --> 00:01:06,500
Tater tots on me.

27
00:01:07,340 --> 00:01:08,840
Rista, grab the other one, would you?

28
00:01:09,020 --> 00:01:09,760
No problem.

29
00:01:09,760 --> 00:01:15,220
Oh, wow.

30
00:01:15,360 --> 00:01:17,520
Being able to fly with you is incredible, Master.

31
00:01:17,740 --> 00:01:19,500
Something doesn't look right up ahead.

32
00:01:19,880 --> 00:01:20,140
Huh?

33
00:01:20,560 --> 00:01:22,040
Maybe it's a rain cloud?

34
00:01:27,160 --> 00:01:29,660
That's a huge swarm of flies.

35
00:01:29,900 --> 00:01:30,420
Gross.

36
00:01:30,420 --> 00:01:37,380
Three to four hundred of those flying poop eaters.

37
00:01:37,760 --> 00:01:38,880
All over level 30.

38
00:01:39,440 --> 00:01:40,560
So the phoenix is out.

39
00:01:41,520 --> 00:01:43,300
Let's stay back and see what happens.

40
00:01:43,720 --> 00:01:45,120
Yeah, I'm good with that plan.

41
00:01:45,460 --> 00:01:47,080
Bow down before us, humans.

42
00:01:48,080 --> 00:01:51,720
Tremble at the overwhelming might of the Demon Lord's airborne shock troops.

43
00:01:51,820 --> 00:01:53,160
The aerial assault flies.

44
00:01:53,580 --> 00:01:55,660
I'm thinking that must be the boss bug.

45
00:01:55,660 --> 00:01:59,720
His ability stats kind of suck, so he's not a heavenly king.

46
00:02:01,360 --> 00:02:04,040
That speed rating is kind of out of control, though.

47
00:02:04,260 --> 00:02:05,440
He disgusts me.

48
00:02:05,860 --> 00:02:07,940
I mean, like, how can he talk with that mouth?

49
00:02:08,060 --> 00:02:09,260
I don't even want to know.

50
00:02:11,260 --> 00:02:14,220
How does that help us counteract his stupid fast feet?

51
00:02:14,280 --> 00:02:15,080
Look over there.

52
00:02:15,300 --> 00:02:17,440
Those Rose Guard soldiers are being targeted.

53
00:02:17,940 --> 00:02:18,280
Release!

54
00:02:18,280 --> 00:02:28,600
It looks like even the minion flies all have pretty decent evasive skills as well.

55
00:02:34,240 --> 00:02:38,680
Now, it's time for something I like to call reverse fireworks.

56
00:02:39,620 --> 00:02:40,380
Say what now?

57
00:02:40,720 --> 00:02:41,500
I don't get it.

58
00:02:41,500 --> 00:02:56,180
I was thinking about calling them Beelbub's blood bombs, but that seems corny.

59
00:02:57,020 --> 00:02:57,380
Hmm.

60
00:02:57,560 --> 00:02:59,360
There's no fire, but you get the idea.

61
00:02:59,820 --> 00:03:01,020
Now, where's that hero?

62
00:03:01,200 --> 00:03:02,900
Is this not enough to draw him out?

63
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:04,080
I can kill more.

64
00:03:04,240 --> 00:03:05,380
I can do this all day.

65
00:03:05,420 --> 00:03:05,940
Am I right?

66
00:03:05,940 --> 00:03:12,160
I wondered why the fortress hadn't fallen, but he basically just told us what was up,

67
00:03:12,220 --> 00:03:12,980
so that's helpful.

68
00:03:13,200 --> 00:03:15,240
I love it when they just tell us like that.

69
00:03:15,420 --> 00:03:19,040
Master, are we going to stand around here and watch, or are we going to swat these flies?

70
00:03:19,360 --> 00:03:20,220
Slow your roll, Turbo.

71
00:03:20,780 --> 00:03:24,560
Normal flies move faster than the blink of an eye, and these are some kind of demon flies,

72
00:03:24,660 --> 00:03:26,720
so they probably move unbelievably quickly.

73
00:03:27,060 --> 00:03:28,360
Now's not the time to act.

74
00:03:28,360 --> 00:03:37,740
Elulu, stay behind me, okay?

75
00:03:37,740 --> 00:03:37,820
Okay?

76
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:52,580
Oh, thank goodness!

77
00:03:52,980 --> 00:03:54,140
You've come at last!

78
00:03:54,140 --> 00:03:58,660
Listen up, soldiers!

79
00:03:58,940 --> 00:04:01,700
The hero and goddess have finally arrived to save our world!

80
00:04:01,920 --> 00:04:02,900
Now stand tall!

81
00:04:03,180 --> 00:04:04,800
Prepare to storm the demon's lair!

82
00:04:04,900 --> 00:04:06,860
Captain Rosalie, please calm yourself.

83
00:04:07,280 --> 00:04:09,560
First, we need to regroup and let the men rest.

84
00:04:09,700 --> 00:04:13,000
We can rest only after we've avenged our fallen brothers in arms.

85
00:04:13,340 --> 00:04:17,720
I know the thirst for blood vengeance well, but you must realize the situation we're in.

86
00:04:17,720 --> 00:04:20,080
Our remaining soldiers are beyond exhausted.

87
00:04:20,740 --> 00:04:23,020
Besides, the hero's just barely arrived.

88
00:04:24,140 --> 00:04:25,900
I suppose you have a point, Carlo.

89
00:04:26,380 --> 00:04:27,580
Let's head back to the fortress.

90
00:04:27,960 --> 00:04:31,580
There we can discuss a strategy to finally defeat these flies with our hero.

91
00:04:31,920 --> 00:04:33,000
Captain Rosalie!

92
00:04:33,200 --> 00:04:35,840
However, once that meeting is done, we're heading back out.

93
00:04:36,260 --> 00:04:37,680
That is an order, you understand?

94
00:04:38,500 --> 00:04:39,680
What are you waiting for?

95
00:04:39,780 --> 00:04:40,160
Move it!

96
00:04:40,340 --> 00:04:41,400
Yes, ma'am!

97
00:04:41,400 --> 00:04:47,720
Wow, that place is massive!

98
00:04:48,720 --> 00:04:51,720
Olga Fortress is at a strategic location on the Imperial border.

99
00:04:52,100 --> 00:04:56,780
In addition to strong walls, the garrison's elite archers are stationed up in the ramparts.

100
00:04:57,560 --> 00:05:00,440
Well, those flies could definitely break through if they wanted.

101
00:05:00,700 --> 00:05:02,940
Clearly, their objective was to lure you here.

102
00:05:03,280 --> 00:05:05,280
They wouldn't go any further than the fortress.

103
00:05:05,280 --> 00:05:09,380
But even if they did, the Empire is protected by the Great War Master.

104
00:05:09,940 --> 00:05:10,680
Who's that?

105
00:05:11,360 --> 00:05:12,720
His name really says it all.

106
00:05:13,020 --> 00:05:15,420
He's the greatest living warrior in Gaea Brande.

107
00:05:15,560 --> 00:05:18,500
Yeah, if that were true, he could be saving the world instead of me.

108
00:05:18,960 --> 00:05:19,920
I don't buy the hype.

109
00:05:20,920 --> 00:05:23,300
Forgive me, but present company excluded.

110
00:05:23,960 --> 00:05:28,300
The War Master's absolutely, without a doubt, the mightiest man to ever walk this land.

111
00:05:28,520 --> 00:05:30,360
However, he can't leave the capital.

112
00:05:30,360 --> 00:05:33,580
Captain Rosalie, must you be on the battlefront?

113
00:05:33,820 --> 00:05:36,380
You are next in line to the Imperial Throne, after all!

114
00:05:36,640 --> 00:05:38,600
Which is why I should be in harm's way.

115
00:05:38,960 --> 00:05:40,180
I'm my father's daughter.

116
00:05:40,580 --> 00:05:41,540
A true warrior.

117
00:05:42,240 --> 00:05:43,540
Um, excuse me.

118
00:05:43,780 --> 00:05:44,420
They're here.

119
00:05:44,700 --> 00:05:47,400
The hero and his courageous party have now arrived.

120
00:05:47,720 --> 00:05:49,360
Oh, your greatness is inspiring.

121
00:05:50,080 --> 00:05:51,440
We do appreciate your help.

122
00:05:51,480 --> 00:05:52,520
Come and have a seat.

123
00:05:54,100 --> 00:05:59,260
So, without further ado, we must formulate a strategy at once to eliminate these flies.

124
00:05:59,260 --> 00:06:00,840
Slow down, big guy.

125
00:06:01,220 --> 00:06:03,180
I would like to guarantee our safety first.

126
00:06:03,480 --> 00:06:06,440
One of the Demon Lord's henchmen could be right here with us in disguise.

127
00:06:07,040 --> 00:06:08,420
Wait, do you think so?

128
00:06:08,840 --> 00:06:11,040
All I'm saying is the possibility exists.

129
00:06:11,380 --> 00:06:13,740
Well, I suppose there's a remote chance.

130
00:06:14,360 --> 00:06:18,800
Besides, even if the enemy's not here, they could have planted a bomb to blow us all to hell.

131
00:06:19,060 --> 00:06:20,160
There's a bomb in here?

132
00:06:20,360 --> 00:06:22,700
All I'm saying is the possibility exists.

133
00:06:23,100 --> 00:06:25,020
Yes, I suppose it does.

134
00:06:25,020 --> 00:06:30,000
But even if there's not, I'm almost positive someone's listening in on this meeting.

135
00:06:33,100 --> 00:06:34,960
Carlo, search the ceiling now!

136
00:06:35,380 --> 00:06:35,740
Right!

137
00:06:37,220 --> 00:06:43,800
Sir, 23 soldiers have searched high and low, but the entire area above this room is not only empty, but remarkably clean.

138
00:06:43,940 --> 00:06:45,560
There's no sign of an intruder, sir.

139
00:06:45,780 --> 00:06:46,180
Huh?

140
00:06:46,180 --> 00:06:49,180
All I said was the possibility exists.

141
00:06:49,920 --> 00:06:51,160
I've had enough of this!

142
00:06:51,700 --> 00:06:54,960
What's more than just a possibility is we are not getting any fighting done!

143
00:06:55,280 --> 00:06:56,980
We don't even need to strategize.

144
00:06:57,140 --> 00:06:59,980
The hero and I will stand at the fore and charge into the creature's lair!

145
00:07:00,120 --> 00:07:00,740
That's that!

146
00:07:01,120 --> 00:07:02,800
But Captain Rosalie, we can't be!

147
00:07:03,100 --> 00:07:03,700
She's right.

148
00:07:04,180 --> 00:07:04,460
Huh?

149
00:07:05,140 --> 00:07:05,580
Oh!

150
00:07:05,880 --> 00:07:07,560
So you agree we should charge in?

151
00:07:07,680 --> 00:07:08,900
Don't put words in my mouth.

152
00:07:09,160 --> 00:07:12,040
What I agree with is this meeting is totally pointless.

153
00:07:12,420 --> 00:07:14,600
I know what my next course of action needs to be.

154
00:07:14,600 --> 00:07:16,840
So what do you plan to do?

155
00:07:18,740 --> 00:07:19,640
To leave.

156
00:07:20,540 --> 00:07:20,840
Huh?

157
00:07:21,680 --> 00:07:22,160
Ah!

158
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:25,560
I'm gonna go back to the Divine Room.

159
00:07:25,560 --> 00:07:26,380
Of course that's it.

160
00:07:26,860 --> 00:07:28,260
A classic Sia move.

161
00:07:29,560 --> 00:07:32,160
In here I was getting excited to start an adventure.

162
00:07:32,400 --> 00:07:33,360
This is utterly ridiculous!

163
00:07:34,080 --> 00:07:34,980
You're kidding, right?

164
00:07:35,200 --> 00:07:35,960
I'm never kidding.

165
00:07:36,300 --> 00:07:37,140
It's not my style.

166
00:07:37,240 --> 00:07:39,060
You're seriously going to abandon us?

167
00:07:39,080 --> 00:07:39,740
Cut the drama.

168
00:07:39,980 --> 00:07:40,720
I'm just leaving.

169
00:07:40,800 --> 00:07:41,300
But why?

170
00:07:41,320 --> 00:07:42,140
Makes no sense.

171
00:07:42,260 --> 00:07:42,840
He's chicken?

172
00:07:43,200 --> 00:07:44,520
Well, he's not a hero.

173
00:07:44,800 --> 00:07:45,660
Everyone relax.

174
00:07:45,740 --> 00:07:46,500
I speak Sia.

175
00:07:46,740 --> 00:07:48,680
He doesn't mean going off to train for long.

176
00:07:48,980 --> 00:07:50,680
Probably no more than three days.

177
00:07:50,740 --> 00:07:51,420
What the hell?

178
00:07:51,820 --> 00:07:54,020
But the fortress will be destroyed at that time.

179
00:07:54,080 --> 00:07:54,700
No, listen.

180
00:07:54,900 --> 00:07:57,480
In the Divine Realm, three days is like an hour or so.

181
00:07:57,800 --> 00:07:58,940
That's not too unreasonable.

182
00:07:59,160 --> 00:08:01,180
But why would you even need to train for this fight?

183
00:08:01,520 --> 00:08:03,980
I saw the goddess's wings with my own two eyes.

184
00:08:04,260 --> 00:08:06,020
If you can already fly, you're ready.

185
00:08:06,200 --> 00:08:06,460
Huh?

186
00:08:06,600 --> 00:08:07,020
Who, me?

187
00:08:07,260 --> 00:08:08,320
Goddesses don't fight.

188
00:08:08,440 --> 00:08:09,200
They only support.

189
00:08:09,200 --> 00:08:12,220
Oh, is he actually sticking up for me?

190
00:08:12,840 --> 00:08:13,740
But don't get me wrong.

191
00:08:13,820 --> 00:08:14,900
She's completely useless.

192
00:08:15,160 --> 00:08:16,580
She just kind of floats like a balloon.

193
00:08:16,880 --> 00:08:19,460
Now that I think about it, a balloon would be more capable.

194
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:21,900
Hey, I ought to punch your balloons!

195
00:08:22,120 --> 00:08:23,080
Blind's no big deal.

196
00:08:23,160 --> 00:08:23,980
I can do that.

197
00:08:24,160 --> 00:08:25,320
Oh, is that so?

198
00:08:25,440 --> 00:08:26,800
That doesn't make us less screwed.

199
00:08:27,220 --> 00:08:28,960
Look, I was watching the battle earlier.

200
00:08:29,840 --> 00:08:30,140
Wait.

201
00:08:30,620 --> 00:08:31,440
What did you say?

202
00:08:31,940 --> 00:08:32,700
You were watching?

203
00:08:33,660 --> 00:08:36,980
While my soldiers were being slaughtered, you stood there and watched them die?

204
00:08:37,120 --> 00:08:38,180
No, that's not true.

205
00:08:38,460 --> 00:08:40,880
We wanted to help, but at the time it was just too late.

206
00:08:41,160 --> 00:08:42,340
It's not about timing.

207
00:08:42,500 --> 00:08:43,940
It's about helping or not helping.

208
00:08:44,240 --> 00:08:47,280
I want to know if the hero saw what happened and did nothing to help.

209
00:08:47,420 --> 00:08:49,120
That's a dumb question if you ask me.

210
00:08:49,460 --> 00:08:51,340
If nothing will help, why would I do anything?

211
00:08:51,720 --> 00:08:53,480
My men were murdered by demons.

212
00:08:53,760 --> 00:08:54,400
You're a hero.

213
00:08:54,580 --> 00:08:55,620
Doesn't that affect you?

214
00:08:55,620 --> 00:08:57,080
What would change if it did?

215
00:08:57,380 --> 00:08:59,200
Best thing to do was not get freaked out.

216
00:08:59,600 --> 00:09:01,140
Stay calm and keep my guard up.

217
00:09:01,140 --> 00:09:03,620
This hero is hopeless.

218
00:09:04,100 --> 00:09:06,700
By definition, a hero is supposed to be brave.

219
00:09:06,980 --> 00:09:08,180
But you are not a hero.

220
00:09:08,720 --> 00:09:10,080
You're just a mopey coward.

221
00:09:10,640 --> 00:09:11,160
Rosalie!

222
00:09:11,700 --> 00:09:15,680
I know Seiya can come off as an unfeeling jerk who's afraid to get his hands dirty.

223
00:09:16,000 --> 00:09:17,820
But that's how we've made it this far.

224
00:09:18,140 --> 00:09:20,660
He'll kill those demon flies, but only when he knows he's ready.

225
00:09:21,380 --> 00:09:23,100
So would you please just be patient?

226
00:09:23,100 --> 00:09:25,280
This training will only take an hour.

227
00:09:26,240 --> 00:09:27,560
And why should I?

228
00:09:29,080 --> 00:09:30,120
Valid question.

229
00:09:30,120 --> 00:09:33,000
Over a hundred of my men were popped like grapes.

230
00:09:33,960 --> 00:09:35,120
Have some empathy.

231
00:09:35,680 --> 00:09:38,460
I know it's a horrible thing to go through, but...

232
00:09:38,460 --> 00:09:42,540
You can't know how precious life truly is because you don't have to fear death.

233
00:09:42,800 --> 00:09:45,520
Since you're a goddess, it will literally never happen to you.

234
00:09:45,640 --> 00:09:46,700
He kind of got me there.

235
00:09:47,140 --> 00:09:49,520
So don't speak to me on matters of life and death.

236
00:09:49,520 --> 00:09:54,680
You're not exactly coming from some kind of moral high ground, lady.

237
00:09:55,200 --> 00:09:55,940
Say what?

238
00:09:56,500 --> 00:09:58,500
Your men didn't get killed by accident.

239
00:09:58,960 --> 00:10:00,280
All that stuff is on you.

240
00:10:00,940 --> 00:10:05,000
If you had been able to come up with a strategy that didn't suck, they'd still be alive right now.

241
00:10:06,360 --> 00:10:07,360
You scum!

242
00:10:07,520 --> 00:10:08,900
You better take that back!

243
00:10:08,900 --> 00:10:10,340
We should kill you!

244
00:10:10,340 --> 00:10:10,400
We should kill you!

245
00:10:20,240 --> 00:10:21,600
Wow, time out!

246
00:10:21,840 --> 00:10:24,220
Ziya, in what kind of world is hitting a woman ever okay?

247
00:10:24,420 --> 00:10:27,500
You need to get down on your knees and beg or not to kill you now!

248
00:10:27,500 --> 00:10:29,120
How dare you!

249
00:10:31,340 --> 00:10:31,860
Ow!

250
00:10:33,860 --> 00:10:35,240
Oh, you bastard!

251
00:10:36,000 --> 00:10:36,560
Ow!

252
00:10:36,880 --> 00:10:38,140
You slept like a girl!

253
00:10:38,660 --> 00:10:39,940
Oh, you'll pay for this!

254
00:10:44,580 --> 00:10:47,500
Is there no shred of feminism in this day and age?

255
00:10:47,840 --> 00:10:50,880
I knew he was kind of old-fashioned, but this is the bad kind!

256
00:10:51,760 --> 00:10:53,140
All right, that's it!

257
00:10:53,520 --> 00:10:54,460
You are dead!

258
00:10:54,660 --> 00:10:55,860
I'll slice you to pieces!

259
00:10:55,860 --> 00:10:57,880
Captain Rosalie, control yourself!

260
00:10:58,200 --> 00:10:59,040
You're a fraud!

261
00:10:59,620 --> 00:11:00,840
You are not a hero!

262
00:11:01,620 --> 00:11:03,620
You're just a jerk face!

263
00:11:04,060 --> 00:11:05,280
Apologize, you cape man!

264
00:11:05,600 --> 00:11:07,400
Nope, she was coming in hard, bro.

265
00:11:07,740 --> 00:11:08,500
Look at her!

266
00:11:08,580 --> 00:11:09,500
You made her cry!

267
00:11:09,640 --> 00:11:10,300
I know it!

268
00:11:10,460 --> 00:11:11,460
I'm not crying!

269
00:11:11,800 --> 00:11:12,520
You're crying!

270
00:11:13,600 --> 00:11:16,540
The way that I see it, she should be apologizing to me.

271
00:11:16,840 --> 00:11:20,280
The way I see it, you're an embarrassment to men and heroes, so apologize!

272
00:11:20,820 --> 00:11:22,520
I don't need a stupid hero!

273
00:11:22,920 --> 00:11:23,940
Ziya, shut up!

274
00:11:23,940 --> 00:11:25,920
I'll go take care of them myself!

275
00:11:27,700 --> 00:11:30,460
You do have incredibly high strength for a human.

276
00:11:30,620 --> 00:11:33,860
The War Master may be your father, but I guess ability ratings aren't genetic.

277
00:11:34,260 --> 00:11:35,680
You're just gonna get yourself killed.

278
00:11:39,760 --> 00:11:41,560
She's starting to growl like a dog!

279
00:11:41,700 --> 00:11:43,380
Is she gonna turn into a werewolf?

280
00:11:43,380 --> 00:11:45,100
I think she's rabid, so leave her alone.

281
00:11:45,640 --> 00:11:47,880
Hey, Master, are you sure you shouldn't apologize?

282
00:11:48,380 --> 00:11:50,120
I'm sorry, but I don't do apologies.

283
00:11:50,640 --> 00:11:51,260
Open a portal.

284
00:11:51,740 --> 00:11:52,260
Let's go.

285
00:11:52,600 --> 00:11:53,800
Uh, uh, sure.

286
00:11:57,640 --> 00:12:00,580
Yeah, geez, that rally!

287
00:12:01,100 --> 00:12:01,900
Is she a dog?

288
00:12:02,100 --> 00:12:03,560
Okay, find our happy place!

289
00:12:04,020 --> 00:12:05,780
We're leaving, but we'll be back in an hour!

290
00:12:06,080 --> 00:12:07,620
Try not to bite anyone while we're gone!

291
00:12:07,620 --> 00:12:18,780
I know you, um, have your ways, but don't ever do anything like that again!

292
00:12:19,000 --> 00:12:19,880
There's no excuse!

293
00:12:20,340 --> 00:12:22,260
I was scared you were gonna kill each other!

294
00:12:22,260 --> 00:12:23,980
Well, that slapping was pretty intense.

295
00:12:24,480 --> 00:12:25,700
I couldn't stop myself.

296
00:12:26,480 --> 00:12:29,600
It's like all of that crap that she was spewing triggered my slap button.

297
00:12:29,980 --> 00:12:30,700
Don't care.

298
00:12:31,380 --> 00:12:32,840
The way she thinks is BS.

299
00:12:33,380 --> 00:12:35,820
How bent on moving forward when there's no chance of winning.

300
00:12:36,220 --> 00:12:38,680
Besides the casualties, it makes you look like an idiot.

301
00:12:40,580 --> 00:12:40,940
Hmm.

302
00:12:41,460 --> 00:12:44,880
Yeah, it's pretty much the exact opposite approach from how you like to do everything.

303
00:12:45,680 --> 00:12:47,900
So, uh, you feel like taking a little breather?

304
00:12:48,480 --> 00:12:48,880
Great.

305
00:12:49,060 --> 00:12:50,160
Another dumb question.

306
00:12:50,160 --> 00:12:53,620
I figured out how to deal with that demon bug infestation.

307
00:12:53,820 --> 00:12:57,440
Well, if you need one of the gods around here to help you with something, I can hook you up.

308
00:12:57,740 --> 00:13:00,120
Like the god of Patriot's surface-to-air missiles?

309
00:13:00,280 --> 00:13:00,500
What?

310
00:13:00,680 --> 00:13:01,920
There's no god for that!

311
00:13:02,080 --> 00:13:03,340
How about the god of guns?

312
00:13:03,700 --> 00:13:05,700
We might actually have one of those somewhere.

313
00:13:06,100 --> 00:13:09,120
But although Gabriente has a lot of ways to kill, there are no guns.

314
00:13:09,680 --> 00:13:11,940
If we're the only ones with guns, we win.

315
00:13:12,240 --> 00:13:14,360
Listen, Saya, it's just not gonna happen!

316
00:13:14,620 --> 00:13:16,600
Guns literally do not exist there!

317
00:13:16,840 --> 00:13:19,160
Well, if the guns and Patriot missiles are out...

318
00:13:19,160 --> 00:13:21,320
...that leaves us with bows.

319
00:13:22,200 --> 00:13:22,540
Great!

320
00:13:22,660 --> 00:13:24,180
Because I know the goddess of archery.

321
00:13:24,540 --> 00:13:26,920
She's in the verdant forest, which is a little ways from here.

322
00:13:27,420 --> 00:13:27,740
Cool.

323
00:13:27,860 --> 00:13:28,300
Let's go.

324
00:13:28,900 --> 00:13:30,360
Maybe she can teach me something.

325
00:13:34,500 --> 00:13:35,020
Hmm!

326
00:13:35,180 --> 00:13:36,700
She's practicing right up ahead!

327
00:13:36,700 --> 00:13:48,820
Please pardon the interruption, Metis.

328
00:13:49,380 --> 00:13:51,400
Oh, Ristarte, I don't see you here often.

329
00:13:52,060 --> 00:13:53,700
Is there something I can help you with today?

330
00:13:54,080 --> 00:13:57,740
Well, I was telling my hero friend here about your amazing skill as an archer,

331
00:13:57,800 --> 00:14:00,940
and we were hoping you wouldn't mind sharing a few tips with him to up his game.

332
00:14:01,080 --> 00:14:04,060
You're supposed to be the best, so how many arrows can you shoot at once?

333
00:14:04,060 --> 00:14:05,840
Ever heard of buttering someone at first?

334
00:14:05,940 --> 00:14:08,860
It isn't really possible to shoot more than one arrow at a time,

335
00:14:09,020 --> 00:14:12,240
but I can shoot in quick succession to mimic simultaneous fire.

336
00:14:22,560 --> 00:14:23,500
Shining arrow.

337
00:14:23,500 --> 00:14:33,240
That was so fast, I bet the tree never even saw it coming!

338
00:14:33,580 --> 00:14:36,780
After centuries of training, seven quick shots is my limit.

339
00:14:37,180 --> 00:14:38,040
Just seven shots?

340
00:14:38,340 --> 00:14:40,020
How about hitting something that actually moves?

341
00:14:40,100 --> 00:14:40,960
Do you think you'd miss?

342
00:14:41,480 --> 00:14:42,300
Um, no.

343
00:14:42,460 --> 00:14:43,400
That would never happen.

344
00:14:43,940 --> 00:14:44,360
Really?

345
00:14:44,540 --> 00:14:46,580
I wouldn't be the goddess of archery if I missed.

346
00:14:46,920 --> 00:14:50,760
Unfortunately, that kind of speed and precision is impossible for humans like you.

347
00:14:50,760 --> 00:14:53,840
Yeah, we'll see. Why don't you teach me a thing or two first?

348
00:14:54,420 --> 00:14:57,240
Before we begin, you need to be able to use a magic bow.

349
00:14:57,740 --> 00:15:02,740
If that proves to be too much, there are other types of lessons I'd love to teach you, personally.

350
00:15:03,700 --> 00:15:04,920
Send me what I think it means!

351
00:15:04,980 --> 00:15:06,680
I just want to learn how to use the bow.

352
00:15:08,240 --> 00:15:11,720
Elulu, you know how to use fire arrow, don't you? Teach it to me.

353
00:15:11,800 --> 00:15:15,620
You're good at a lot of things, Ziya, but I don't know if you can just pick it up just like that!

354
00:15:15,960 --> 00:15:16,860
Just do it, okay?

355
00:15:16,860 --> 00:15:22,680
The first step is to stretch out your left hand and visualize a flaming magic bow in it.

356
00:15:22,820 --> 00:15:23,320
Like this?

357
00:15:23,340 --> 00:15:24,920
Now picture an arrow in your right hand.

358
00:15:25,280 --> 00:15:26,840
You're going too fast!

359
00:15:27,040 --> 00:15:30,220
But the next step is really the toughest part of the whole process.

360
00:15:30,540 --> 00:15:33,340
Hitting the target is where all of the skills start to come in!

361
00:15:35,840 --> 00:15:36,800
That was easy.

362
00:15:37,540 --> 00:15:39,340
Well, for you, maybe.

363
00:15:39,340 --> 00:15:42,720
My word, you are surprisingly quick to catch on.

364
00:15:42,960 --> 00:15:44,520
I understand why she chose you.

365
00:15:44,860 --> 00:15:47,060
I'd be happy to start training you right away.

366
00:15:49,220 --> 00:15:50,820
Well, there goes my dignity.

367
00:15:51,660 --> 00:15:52,980
Don't let it bother you.

368
00:15:53,120 --> 00:15:54,260
That guy's a freak of nature.

369
00:15:54,360 --> 00:15:57,580
Well, since we're waiting on him, how do you suggest we pass the time?

370
00:15:57,860 --> 00:15:58,980
What did Ziya tell you?

371
00:15:58,980 --> 00:16:02,540
You kids can go to the cafeteria and eat candy or whatever the hell you do.

372
00:16:03,440 --> 00:16:04,480
Sounds like him.

373
00:16:05,100 --> 00:16:09,560
I don't want to just sit around, so could you introduce me to a god who'll help me get stronger?

374
00:16:10,000 --> 00:16:11,920
Yeah, I don't mind finding someone for you.

375
00:16:12,200 --> 00:16:13,080
Do you want one, too?

376
00:16:13,900 --> 00:16:15,040
Nah, not today.

377
00:16:15,520 --> 00:16:17,080
I'm going to do the candy plan.

378
00:16:17,560 --> 00:16:18,360
I'll join you.

379
00:16:18,360 --> 00:16:20,160
What do you say we eat some macarons?

380
00:16:20,400 --> 00:16:21,040
That sound good?

381
00:16:21,140 --> 00:16:22,620
Hey, look, it's Circeus.

382
00:16:24,080 --> 00:16:25,480
Hey there, big fella.

383
00:16:26,120 --> 00:16:26,720
Oh, no.

384
00:16:26,980 --> 00:16:30,300
If you're here, that means that psychopath's here, too, isn't he?

385
00:16:30,480 --> 00:16:32,780
Ziya's training in the Divine Forest right now.

386
00:16:33,020 --> 00:16:33,900
Did something happen?

387
00:16:34,860 --> 00:16:35,940
Are you kidding me?

388
00:16:36,040 --> 00:16:39,180
Or did you forget about all the stuff that went down with him and Nadinella last time?

389
00:16:39,300 --> 00:16:42,040
She's a wreck to begin with, and now she's ten times worse.

390
00:16:42,360 --> 00:16:43,940
Totally slipped my mind.

391
00:16:45,240 --> 00:16:47,320
So what has she been doing, exactly?

392
00:16:47,320 --> 00:16:47,540
What?

393
00:16:47,840 --> 00:16:51,620
S-S-S-Saya, I'm going to c-c-kill you.

394
00:16:51,780 --> 00:16:53,320
She skulks around like that all day.

395
00:16:53,480 --> 00:16:56,000
It's like hearing the worst hip-hop DJ ever.

396
00:16:56,460 --> 00:16:57,520
It's that bad, huh?

397
00:16:57,540 --> 00:16:57,820
It is.

398
00:16:57,860 --> 00:16:59,120
It's really not funny anymore.

399
00:16:59,520 --> 00:17:02,660
If she sees him around, she's definitely going to gut him like a fish.

400
00:17:04,800 --> 00:17:06,400
I'd heard she was upset.

401
00:17:07,120 --> 00:17:10,020
I tried to cheer her up a bit, but she didn't want to listen to me.

402
00:17:10,020 --> 00:17:13,520
I wonder if Ishtar could talk to her and try to smooth things out a little.

403
00:17:14,400 --> 00:17:15,820
I'd keep her out of this.

404
00:17:15,820 --> 00:17:17,840
I'm just afraid Seiya's going to get shanked.

405
00:17:18,200 --> 00:17:20,820
Nadinella's strange, but she'd never do that.

406
00:17:21,120 --> 00:17:25,440
And in the unlikely case she did, knowing that hero, he wouldn't even be phased.

407
00:17:25,580 --> 00:17:27,480
Well, I don't really want to test that theory!

408
00:17:27,900 --> 00:17:32,580
Not to mention go through all of this with him just to have him get killed by some side-eyeing golf goddess with a grudge!

409
00:17:32,580 --> 00:17:36,000
I'm guessing she's not the best goddess to ask to help with my training, huh?

410
00:17:36,160 --> 00:17:37,580
But what should I do instead?

411
00:17:38,280 --> 00:17:40,400
If you stay here, it's all you can eat, can you?

412
00:17:40,720 --> 00:17:43,680
Young man, I can sense that you have some dormant powers.

413
00:17:44,200 --> 00:17:46,200
You mean the dragon god Metamorphosis?

414
00:17:46,620 --> 00:17:49,980
They say if I can work hard enough, I'll be able to turn into a dragon.

415
00:17:50,380 --> 00:17:51,760
Sounds like you have a seal.

416
00:17:52,100 --> 00:17:54,260
If you want my help, I can release it for you.

417
00:17:54,520 --> 00:17:55,860
For real? You could do that?

418
00:17:55,860 --> 00:17:59,100
I'm all for learning new things, but that sounds like cheating to me.

419
00:17:59,340 --> 00:18:03,100
I'm just teaching him the proper way to unlock a power he already possesses.

420
00:18:03,320 --> 00:18:04,520
It's another form of training.

421
00:18:04,980 --> 00:18:07,760
Okay, if you say it's fine, then knock yourself out.

422
00:18:07,920 --> 00:18:09,440
Don't worry about me, Rista.

423
00:18:09,980 --> 00:18:12,400
I'll just keep doing what I'm best at, which is shoveling candy.

424
00:18:12,980 --> 00:18:16,160
Oh, I can see that you have some hidden talents as well.

425
00:18:16,480 --> 00:18:18,660
I would be able to draw them out for you if you'd like.

426
00:18:18,660 --> 00:18:22,140
Oh, really? If you think I could do something cool, then teach me.

427
00:18:22,280 --> 00:18:24,760
Draw it out, drag it out, rip it out, whatever you need to do.

428
00:18:24,760 --> 00:18:26,980
Ari is always the best for a good pick-me-up.

429
00:18:27,220 --> 00:18:28,720
She even sees potential in Ailulu.

430
00:18:30,320 --> 00:18:33,480
I'm sure she's right that Aranella is just a harmless wackadoodle.

431
00:18:34,860 --> 00:18:38,400
But still, I think it's best for me to go and talk her down a little.

432
00:18:38,720 --> 00:18:41,500
Hey, sweetie, it's your old friend Rista checking in.

433
00:18:43,840 --> 00:18:45,040
Are you home?

434
00:18:47,180 --> 00:18:50,540
I guess she's out.

435
00:18:54,760 --> 00:18:57,960
Oh, she's out.

436
00:18:58,140 --> 00:18:59,000
Out of her mind!

437
00:19:03,760 --> 00:19:07,120
Starte, if you're back here, the matter means one thing.

438
00:19:07,340 --> 00:19:09,980
Your tight-bodied friend is back here, too.

439
00:19:11,360 --> 00:19:13,500
No, I came all by myself this time.

440
00:19:13,540 --> 00:19:14,760
I don't know where he is.

441
00:19:15,040 --> 00:19:16,520
Oh, is that true?

442
00:19:16,860 --> 00:19:17,240
Really?

443
00:19:17,600 --> 00:19:19,180
Oh, yeah, I haven't seen him in a while.

444
00:19:19,180 --> 00:19:21,260
So, what do you need, anyway?

445
00:19:21,600 --> 00:19:22,300
It's nothing.

446
00:19:22,420 --> 00:19:23,640
Don't even worry about it.

447
00:19:23,660 --> 00:19:25,260
Then why did you come in?

448
00:19:25,520 --> 00:19:28,060
Oh, well, I was just looking for some decorating inspirations.

449
00:19:28,140 --> 00:19:29,500
You've got such a unique style.

450
00:19:29,740 --> 00:19:32,120
But I'm not sure I can pull this off as well.

451
00:19:33,240 --> 00:19:33,640
Yeah?

452
00:19:34,020 --> 00:19:34,460
Really?

453
00:19:39,100 --> 00:19:39,500
Tanya!

454
00:19:41,400 --> 00:19:42,500
So, how's it going?

455
00:19:43,140 --> 00:19:46,040
She's done training me, but I should have it totally mastered by tomorrow.

456
00:19:46,200 --> 00:19:46,740
Maybe sooner.

457
00:19:46,940 --> 00:19:48,000
That's awesome, anyway!

458
00:19:48,320 --> 00:19:51,540
Just make sure you don't set foot outside this forest and run into Adanella, got it?

459
00:19:51,760 --> 00:19:53,320
And why should I be worried about that?

460
00:19:53,320 --> 00:19:55,760
Just do what I'm asking you to do for once, okay?

461
00:19:55,900 --> 00:19:58,280
I'll bring the shorties back here tomorrow and we'll leave!

462
00:19:58,440 --> 00:20:00,460
You're way more annoying than usual today.

463
00:20:00,660 --> 00:20:02,120
So, what crawled up your butt?

464
00:20:02,240 --> 00:20:05,540
Please, I'm just asking that you stay here and try not to run into Adanella.

465
00:20:05,960 --> 00:20:08,540
Do you really not know that she's standing right behind you?

466
00:20:08,540 --> 00:20:16,940
I'm just asking that you're lying to me.

467
00:20:18,080 --> 00:20:21,840
So, I decided to follow you here and find out the truth.

468
00:20:21,880 --> 00:20:23,340
Hold on there, just take it easy!

469
00:20:23,440 --> 00:20:24,440
I can explain everything!

470
00:20:24,580 --> 00:20:25,320
Just calm down!

471
00:20:25,400 --> 00:20:25,920
It's okay!

472
00:20:26,460 --> 00:20:28,020
Now, I'll kill him.

473
00:20:28,260 --> 00:20:29,300
Yes, I will.

474
00:20:29,740 --> 00:20:31,040
He's gonna pay!

475
00:20:31,780 --> 00:20:34,360
Oh no, that's the Adanella sword stance.

476
00:20:34,600 --> 00:20:36,020
She did not come here to play.

477
00:20:36,020 --> 00:20:42,420
Go on and draw your blade if you're man enough to fight against a woman who's ten times the warrior you are.

478
00:20:43,740 --> 00:20:45,240
Hey, I know you're fine.

479
00:20:45,720 --> 00:20:46,580
But how are you doing?

480
00:20:46,760 --> 00:20:47,620
Long time no see.

481
00:20:47,920 --> 00:20:49,280
What are you talking about?

482
00:20:49,580 --> 00:20:54,340
You can't treat me like you did the other day and just expect me to act like nothing happened.

483
00:20:54,760 --> 00:20:55,860
You gotta pay!

484
00:20:56,080 --> 00:20:57,480
What is up with your hair?

485
00:20:58,780 --> 00:21:00,200
Something the matter with it?

486
00:21:00,200 --> 00:21:04,940
She's gonna pierce your spleen, you idiot!

487
00:21:05,580 --> 00:21:07,260
You do own a comb, don't you?

488
00:21:07,580 --> 00:21:11,300
S-s-stop touching me with your warm, manly hands like that.

489
00:21:11,320 --> 00:21:12,180
Now isn't that better?

490
00:21:12,540 --> 00:21:12,900
Hey!

491
00:21:13,060 --> 00:21:14,500
Come on, Captain Battery Issues!

492
00:21:14,900 --> 00:21:15,760
You-you...

493
00:21:15,760 --> 00:21:20,880
I-I-I-I-I-I-I forgive you.

494
00:21:21,980 --> 00:21:22,360
Eh?

495
00:21:22,900 --> 00:21:24,940
What happened to all that psycho rage?

496
00:21:25,020 --> 00:21:26,440
Did he pin it out of you?

497
00:21:26,760 --> 00:21:28,440
I-I just can't help myself.

498
00:21:28,620 --> 00:21:31,360
It's cliched, but I can't stay mad at someone so hot.

499
00:21:32,240 --> 00:21:34,560
Adanella, I need to get back to my training.

500
00:21:34,940 --> 00:21:37,280
You being here is distracting and it brings me down.

501
00:21:37,540 --> 00:21:38,980
So hurry on out of here now.

502
00:21:38,980 --> 00:21:40,500
Uh-uh-all right.

503
00:21:40,800 --> 00:21:41,680
L-love you.

504
00:21:42,640 --> 00:21:44,300
Wow, that's horrible.

505
00:21:44,880 --> 00:21:47,580
I mean, he's hot, I get it, but have some self-respect.

506
00:21:48,740 --> 00:21:51,480
Knowing that hero, he wouldn't even be fazed.

507
00:21:51,920 --> 00:21:53,460
Yeah, she really called that one.

508
00:21:54,280 --> 00:21:55,780
Maybe I'll get carried away.

509
00:21:57,860 --> 00:21:58,880
Out of the way.

510
00:21:59,260 --> 00:22:00,220
I'm training here.

511
00:22:04,220 --> 00:22:04,360
Hmm.

512
00:22:08,980 --> 00:22:38,960
Out of the way.

513
00:22:38,980 --> 00:23:08,960
Out of the way.

514
00:23:08,980 --> 00:23:10,360
繋いだ糸

515
00:23:10,360 --> 00:23:14,760
遠く細いけど輝いた絆

516
00:23:14,760 --> 00:23:17,660
確かめた追いつけない

517
00:23:17,660 --> 00:23:19,100
オラバラスライ

518
00:23:19,100 --> 00:23:20,640
刻んでそっと

519
00:23:20,640 --> 00:23:22,060
痛いな一歩

520
00:23:22,060 --> 00:23:25,380
